        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_21.lnote.la.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">646</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fridb. <hi rend="italic">Lb Va Ph</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fridb. Lb Va Ph</seg></note>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude-crib" ana="#fromLatin">That (archbishops, bishops, earls and barons and) all who have sake and soke and toll and team and infangentheof ought to give frankpledges (for their knights, officers and dependants and) for all who serve them. (Archbishops, bishops, earls,) barons (and all who have sake and soke, toll and team and infangentheof) should also have their knights and their own servants, namely stewards, butlers, chamberlains, cooks, bakers, under their own frankpledge; and these likewise their squires or others serving them under their frankpledge.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_21.lnote.oe.erkl-rs" n="Rs" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Rubrik wie Lond I 646 <hi rend="superscript">30</hi><hi rend="italic">De bar. qui s. h. cu. et cons.</hi> — nur <hi rend="italic">barones</hi>, ohne <hi rend="italic">A.</hi><hi rend="superscript">1</hi> <hi rend="italic">e. c.</hi> oder <hi rend="italic">et</hi><hi rend="superscript">3</hi> bis <hi rend="italic">inf.</hi><hi rend="superscript">8</hi> — <hi rend="italic">sub friborgo</hi><hi rend="superscript">19</hi>, dahinter <hi rend="italic">suo</hi> übergeschr. Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Rubric as Lond I 646 <hi rend="superscript">30</hi><hi rend="italic">De bar. qui s. h. cu. et cons.</hi> — only <hi rend="italic">barones</hi>, without <hi rend="italic">A.</hi><hi rend="superscript">1</hi> <hi rend="italic">e. c.</hi> or <hi rend="italic">et</hi><hi rend="superscript">3</hi> to <hi rend="italic">inf.</hi><hi rend="superscript">8</hi> — <hi rend="italic">sub friborgo</hi><hi rend="superscript">19</hi>, after it <hi rend="italic">suo</hi> written above the line, Rs</seg></note>
      </div>
